menu "JrBot V2 - hardware"
    config JR_HEADLESS_DIAGNOSTIC
        bool "Run without OLED (no I2C access to GPIO1/2)"
        default y
        help
            Leaves the OLED disconnected from the software while keeping the
            command terminal and Wi-Fi available. No peripheral starts a test
            automatically. Power off before disconnecting a suspect OLED.

    config JR_AUDIO_PINS_CONFIRMED
        bool "Allow MAX98357A test after verifying GPIO39/40/41"
        default n
        help
            Verify BCLK=39, WS/LRC=40, ESP32 DOUT to amplifier DIN=41.
            These GPIOs must be exposed and free, including external JTAG.
            This enables audio_test; it does not start audio at boot.

    config JR_CAMERA_PINS_CONFIRMED
        bool "Allow one-shot camera test after verifying the existing camera pinout"
        default n
        help
            Only for the camera wiring documented in jr_board.h and
            DIAGNOSTICO_SEM_OLED.md. No autofocus or servo movement.
            camera_test initializes the sensor, obtains one QVGA JPEG frame
            and deinitializes the camera. A valid frame is not an optical test.
endmenu
